## Flight report

- **Left gate:** crossed during the k=8 straight-through move (decision k=9's view showed the signature transit: posts gone from the forward panel, open room beyond, crossbar/base stripe passed underneath in the downward panel). The crossing was through the middle — both posts were visible with the gap on the centre tick before the straight advance, per R6. Getting lined up took many corrections (k=1–k=7): I repeatedly got too close to the near post (R5 reverse/turn-away cycles) before finally getting a clean centred view.
- **Center gate:** never found. After the left-gate transit I advanced ~1m along +x (R7 buffer) then spent the remaining decisions (k=10–k=13) turning and sweeping right/left across roughly -8° to -48° heading while advancing deeper into the room (final pose x=5.59, y=-0.96). Only room clutter (a mannequin, shelving, boxes/crates) was ever in view — no second gate posts appeared.
- **Penguin:** never located. No black-and-white shape was seen in the downward camera during the second-gate search.
- **Final pose:** x=5.59, y=-0.96, z=1.50, heading≈-18° (after the final +30° turn away from the wall clutter, ending the flight without closing distance on the obstruction).
- **Outcome:** did not finish. First gate crossed cleanly through the middle; second gate was never located within the 14-decision budget, so the penguin hover was never attempted. A large share of decisions (roughly half) were spent recovering from over/under-turning while lining up on the first gate, which left too few decisions to search out the second gate and the penguin.
